Subject: CPMS I03B Faithful JSON Byte Ingress Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 0e46c0a3-7c9a-4b29-ab87-f4dc0b748c55

& [Need] ordinary object parsing can collapse duplicate keys and numeric spelling before independent readers observe the supplied instance
& [Selected] one bounded iterative byte scanner before serde and schema validation
  + preserves exact bytes and number spans
  + proves strict UTF-8 one value duplicate absence and finite work
  + returns one accepted instance or one atomic stable fault
& [Rejected] serde_json Value as first authority because map construction loses duplicate occurrence evidence
& [Rejected] native recursive descent because the profile requires explicit depth and stack accounting independent of native stack behavior
& [Rejected] Unicode normalization because it would rewrite member identity beyond JSON decoding
& [StricterProfile] unpaired surrogate escapes and BOM are refused deliberately to create portable scalar and framing identity
& [DependencyIndependence] standard library plus existing cantor_core digest support is sufficient; I03A validator activation is not needed for formation
& [Decision] form the scanner contract now and require separate activation before Rust implementation
